!! TW5 Module Interface

A carrier that wears `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/tw5-module` declares its intent to supply a
kernel-injectable TW5 module. The boot gate `bootTrustedModules` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-module-gate.ts`)
queries for every carrier wearing this component (`stack:has`), evaluates the capability threshold, and
adds each passing body as a JavaScript tiddler. `TW5Engine.boot` runs the gate in the host boot callback,
after TW5 completes its own module collection — so execution of a gated body during that boot reads UNBUILT.

!!! Required `#meta` Fields

| field | meaning |
|---|---|
| `content-type` | MUST read `"application/javascript"`; the built gate checks no such field and stamps the injected tiddler's `type` itself |
| `module-type` | MUST name one of `"parser"`, `"widget"`, `"library"`, `"startup"`; the built gate checks no list and reads an absent value as `"library"` |
| `tw5-module-name` | Proposed module registration key (e.g. `"text/memetic-wikitext"` for parsers); UNBUILT — the gate reads no such field, and TW5 registers a tiddler module under its `title` |
| `mana` | MUST reach ≥ 18 to pass gate layer 1 (threshold) |
| `manao` | MUST reach ≥ 17 to pass gate layer 1 (threshold) |
| `manaoio` | MUST reach ≥ 17 to pass gate layer 1 (threshold) |
| `confidence` | MUST reach ≥ 18; UNBUILT as a gate — the built gate reads no `confidence` field |
| `source-sha256` | tagged SHA-256 digest (`sha256:…`) of the module record's `text`; MUST match at inject time (gate layer 2 — content integrity); checked by `scripts/sync-heleuma.ts` during the build, which writes the field only under `--sync-modules --commit` |

!!! Body

The module record's `text` — what the deserializer yields for the carrier — MUST hold a self-contained CJS JS
bundle with no unresolved external imports. The bundle MAY reference `tiddlywiki` as the global `$tw` — the host
TW5 instance provides it at injection time. The gate skips an empty body.

!!! Capability Model

The kernel holds the `$tw.wiki` reference. Injecting a module meme into TW5 hands that reference
to the bundle's execution context. Three gate layers must all pass before the kernel hands `$tw.wiki`
to any meme body:

# ''Threshold'' (`mana` ≥ 18, `manao` ≥ 17, `manaoio` ≥ 17; the built gate reads no `confidence`) — declared intent
# ''Content hash'' (`source-sha256` matches the tagged `sha256(text)`) — body integrity; checked by `scripts/sync-heleuma.ts` during `pnpm --filter @lararium/tw5 build` and verified at inject time; a tampered or stale body fails here
# ''Keyhive capability proof'' — UNBUILT: an Ed25519-signed authorization from a keyhive principal. As built the gate passes on layers 1–2 alone

The built gate skips a meme that fails its level or digest check, and it executes no skipped body; the keyhive proof reads UNBUILT.
The build (`sync-heleuma`) anchors trust for layers 1–2; keyhive anchors layer 3 once built.

!!! Fallback

The gate carries no fallback of its own: when no module meme passes, it injects nothing. In the genesis
boot path the packed `lares-memetic-wikitext` plugin supplies the grammar, and TW5 collects its module
tiddlers natively. No `_registerMemeticParser()` and no `_registerWidgets()` stand in source.

